My two cents, people should do it until they've ascended once that
way.  Conservative scumming is much more educational and teaches many
more good habits than explore mode.  And a sudden "i wonder if..." is
perfectly acceptable, provided you intend to revert to the old save as
soon as your curiosity is satisfied, and then go on, not doing
whatever it is you were worried about trying out -- that is, no taking
exp or items once you find out it's safe to do whatever.

But this was not a post about save scumming.  It was about ascending! 
Congratulations.  I haven't ascended a Wizard yet, but an early game
book of Identify might help.  I like what you said about slowing down,
that's good advice in general.

The "Good luck does not time out" means you had a blessed luckstone. 
When you get luck bonuses they don't go away with time, only with luck
penalties.  Without a luckstone, any luck modifier (positive or
negative) eventually go back to zero.  With a regular luck stone, both
good and bad luck is permanent.  With a blessed stone, bad luck still
returns to zero.  With a cursed stone, good luck returns to zero.

You enchanted magicbane higher than most people do.  The general
consensus is that the weapon's special effects work best when
enchanted at +2.  There are spoilers giving the messy numbers.

